        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Celtic religion</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 550 BCE – c. 600 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Origin</span><span class="info-stat-val">Among the Celtic peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, as a descendant of Proto-Celtic paganism, itself derived from Proto-Indo-European religion; its earliest monumental sculptures, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, date to the 6th and 5th centuries BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founder or early teachers</span><span class="info-stat-val">none: it grew from older Indo-European religion, and many of its gods have cognates in other Indo-European mythologies.</span></div>
