          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Followers today</span><span class="info-stat-val">none: it died out as the Celtic peoples converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> from the 3rd century and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and Ireland from the 5th; Celtic neopaganism, a 20th-century new religious movement, draws on it.</span></div>
